  "details": "# Issue: \n\nThe Opti version of my Avatar is based on my Main version with less things on it and a decimate mesh, they use the same materials though. Problem is, in game the VRAM usage of the opti version is somehow higher than the main one. This also wasn't the case all the time, some time ago the opti version used less than the main version.\n\nMain usage:  \n\n- SDK:           136 MB\n\n- Local Test:  106 MB\n\n- Upload:      106 MB\n\nOpti usage:\n\n- SDK:           113 MB\n\n- Local Test:  90 MB\n\n- Upload:      128 MB\n\nAs you can see the numbers aren't really consistent and vary by **a lot**. The Local Test and Upload of the Main Avatar have the same amount of usage, while the Local Test and Upload of the Opti don't. \n\nSomething with the Server side Avatar Analytics seems to be broken so that *sometimes* the Upload has higher reported usage than the Local Test. (Not to mention the in general completely wrong reports of the SDK)\n\n# Expected Behavior:\n\nTexture Memory usage should be the same everywhere, in the SDK, on Local Test Builds and on Uploads.",
